May, 2025 – Radial Nerve Palsy on left arm
Soon after the below entry I got Radial Nerve Palsy for another bizarre case of my body failing to protect itself via sleeping on the arm. Like the Lasik After-Surgery in the coming entries. It was my left arm to hand. It got better and able to move 100% again by the time I am writing this, though still feeling a little stiffness when I stretch up the fingers. There should be digital records in my messages with my mom on Facebook Messenger about it.

May 25, 2025 – Using RegEx a few times since College for “email format validation” and others
Just a personal curiosity driven investigation after catching news online of a local lawyer publicly calling out that the voting machine software versions in the official records served to the public via the government website and what’s actually showing up on people’s ballots are not the same.
GitHub Repository with the Related Files:
github.com/AVSGamer/May_2025_General_Elections_ACM_File_Hashes_Between_Versions/tree/main
Originally livestreamed on Facebook but got deleted so re-uploaded to YouTube:
youtube.com/watch?v=X60bojJXn4s

MAR. 9, 2025 – DECIDED TO TAKE A BREAK FROM WEB3 GAMING
Decided to take a break from videogames that has cryptocurrencies and YGG which is a Filipino Developer Co-founded Legal Entity of multiple guilds, whose vision is to help gamers learn and earn while playing or doing tasks in the game using the verification of the blockchain integrated into the partnered games. As of writing this I am still in those communities albeit only checking in from time to time if there’s something I wanted to check like some news or updates about the games I spent a good amount of time, effort and involvement in. I mostly expect people to send me a direct private message. This is after getting the prize money from the tournament earlier and to go back to traditional Web2 or games that doesn’t have cryptocurrency for the reason of how blockchain technology is still new and top traditional game producer companies are skeptical of its scalability, I guess. Hence the design of a lot of the Web3 Games at the time wasn’t up to par with the types of games I used to play, which a lot of are not Free-to-Play games. The earning aspect for regular gamers is amazing, that’s not allowed on most web2 games. For about 3 years I was doing this Play-to-Earn and here is the link to my YGG Profile where all my NFTs indicating I have completed the GAP Tasks and claimed the corresponding monetary/crypto reward. This is not the same as online gambling/casino games though I had a share of experience working as OJT for one aspiring to host those. The achievements are supposedly NFTs tied to my YGG account. By that I mean they are still not visible in OpenSea website where you can see NFTs and Cryptocurrencies in a person’s crypto wallet:
yieldguild.io/player/2udu0p4y
YGG-linked-crypto-wallet-on-OpenSea:
opensea.io/0x35d388f6cf504082f59341ee13680b8a64696e85
