FEB. 2, 2025 – THE POTASSIUM IV INJECTION IS Painful
I’ve never felt anything as painful as this so far within a short amount of time. I have a tattoo on my left arm that took 2 sessions to complete. I forgot the metrics given by the diagnosis but let’s just say climbing up 1 step was impossible alone. I would lose all energy from my legs the moment I try to lift myself up then have trouble standing back up. They had to call the ambulance and, in the hospital, administer the IV infusion. It was the IV infusion that was painful, and if I remember correctly, one of my loving aunts took a video recording of that exact moment.
Facebook Post: facebook.com/share/p/1CnnK7fNCf/

Feb. 13, 2025 – Internet connection
Since I moved residence again and realized I might keep moving residences I bought myself a 5G Mobile Router from PLDT and modified its antenna connections to be able to attach a stronger external antenna. Still have this router to this day as backup.
Reference: facebook.com/share/v/1Dp83x6wwr/

jan. 30, 2025 – Near Cabrera Road, Taytay, Rizal, PH
Moved from Montevista Subd., Rizal, PH Apartment to a Noel’s Village apartment per aunt’s referral. 100% living by myself but with support from mother, local relatives and doing crypto/web3. Reason for moving was that landlord’s relative was going to use the space.
Reference: facebook.com/share/p/17wWNR6XSj/

NOV. 20-DEC. 2, 2024 – 3RD PLACE WEB3 PROGRAMMING COMPETITION [PROFESSIONAL TRACK]
During the YPS (Yellow Panther Summit) then re-branded to Yield Guild Games Play Summit, participated as a 2-person team with myself as the sole coder/programmer, the other person who was a college student then had a good proposal for the project we brainstormed on what could be in a 14-Day Programming Competition about Games or Software that can be integrated with cryptocurrencies. We won a cash prize of PHP50,000 as 3rd Placer.
