SEPT. 26, 2024 – SHIN MEGAMI TENSEI: IMAGINE ONLINE
This game used to be officially hosted and published by ATLUS; It’s an MMORPG game that made a lasting impact on my life. I was in homeschooling for 4th Year of my High-School at the time. I played this game a lot back then and where I met online, Aki, a Japanese guy working in the field of IT, he was around 20 years old back then from what I can remember him telling me through the in-game chat system and eventually became part of my Facebook Friends to this day. Now there are some of us who miss this game and want to preserve it so they took it upon themselves to re-host the game. New Moon is the name of the new server that I became an intern for and was part of 1 patch. I was tasked to change some items’ category tags (about 7~ items) and increase their inventory stack sizes and did it with a little help at the start.
New Moon Server’s Home Website:
http://54.39.131.171:3000/home

AUG. 19, 2024 – WINDOWS OS LICENSE UPGRADED
Don’t remember the exact details but I guess at one point I applied to be part of the Windows Insider Program and this is the date of appointment showing in my account. I bought an OEM License Key as it’s cheaper than Physical Installers.

April, 2024 – 1st time doing modification of a SIM Router
Bought a cheap albeit fake GT990+ Pro Sim Router then later modified it to accommodate an external antenna and did the same to a PLDT 5G Router.
Reference: facebook.com/share/p/1BxABNVKG4/

Apr. 5, 2024 - WON MY 2ND RAMEN CARD NFT
Supposedly only 1 Ramen Card per player if they got it from events or promos. But you can buy as much of them as you want from the marketplace. The NFT Card has benefits tied to it which is being able to buy and sell exclusive in-game items (“food buffs” in most games). At initial release the price for that was around $800 and I was one of lucky winners of it then. I decided to not sell mine yet at that price which I later kind of regretted since now I don’t have any of those Ramen Cards though 2 went through my possession. I sold them at around $100; the other was like $250-300. I still log into the game from time to time but only to farm tokens ($1~/6days currently, back then $10/day for me and for others even more). Reference: youtube.com/live/29u_R8qiuRs?t=616s

DEC. 31, 2023 - GENSOKISHI -METAWORLD- VIDEOGAME SPEEDRUN TOURNAMENT CHAMPION
The team compositions were decided randomly in 3 players per team. We won $340 as 1st Place and split it among us evenly. My role in this mostly served as a coordinator for the team to schedule time to practice and collaborate on how we should do the performance.
