July 7, 2023 – Doing my own Haircut
Started doing my own haircut influenced by COVID Pandemic. Depending on the mood I would go semi-bald or undercut on myself.
Reference: facebook.com/share/v/1Aqhjj46Lo/

July, 2023 – Joined YGG (Yield Guild Games)
I became aware of YGG when they started interacting with GensoKishi which was the first web3 videogame that I was really amazed with because so far, all the other play-to-earn I encountered didn’t seem that much profitable and it had better quality as a videogame because of being an official web3 port of the original web2 game from Japan. During this time, I was designated to join the Sub-Guild/Group “ALLGUDSINDAHOOD” later shortened to “ALLGUDS”. Our leader and his girlfriend helped me later on with GCash concerning an issue with my bounced transaction. YGG frequently collaborates with other Philippine Tech Financial companies, such as CoinsPH, GCash, Smart and Smart’s Paymaya, etc. E-wallets that I have accounts on and even attended a one-time demo/seminar with/by invitation of a friend I made from living in the boarding house at Quezon City during my freshman year in T.I.P. QC. Since joining YGG, we’ve been doing a lot of “Airdrops” and “Tasks/Compete/Complete” to earn. While other task-scammers were trying to imitate them. Also became a member of the Game Testers part of YGG.

June, 2023 – Montevista Heighs Subd., Beside Ortigas Ext.
Moved residence from Grandparent’s Ancestral Home to an apartment in Montevista Heights Subd., Reason for leaving is that the ancestral home needs repairing, leakages from the roof, etc. A high school friend introduced me to the landlord of the apartment. Living by myself, it’s pretty easy for me to forgo cleaning much when living by myself even in apartments so I guess it was a bit dirty but I absolutely avoid having anything that may expire or stink. First time experiencing the sink getting clogged by instant noodles by-product liquid and having to re-attach the toilet bowl because a mollusk shell clogged it. Gave my acoustic guitar as a show of appreciation to the guy who worked the toilet, since I think we didn’t really pay him much and he took interest in it. Cool dude said he used to be a dancer too until life happened. I was mostly just a dancer in school settings.

APR. 11, 2023 – GENSOKISHI MONSTER COMPENDIUM
An implementation of a query-able database on Google Sheets with sorting and filtering options. This is not the first time I’ve made this sort of project using Google Sheets. I chose to make it on this platform because it is free and has the capability to be used like so. Coincidentally the game was having an event/contest for UGCs (User Generated Content) so I submitted this as my entry and they did accept, it just didn’t win if I remember correctly. There’s also a Japanese developer who have more advanced tools on their website pertaining to the game. And the goal of creating this has always been a way for myself but also for other players to use it whenever they want to. It’s a self-initiated project, just like a lot of the other coding projects here.
Can be sampled here:
docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1AoOrVXtKCoIY5Fv1FS4sY9G4hTHnqmfLGumQazG5KLI/
I probably should rename that option “Don’t Care” into “Irrelevant”.
My Facebook Post: facebook.com/share/p/1afAWTMgV9/

Dec. 19, 2022 – Finally found a WEB3 VideoGame I liked
I came across a Facebook advertisement/post about this game called GensoKishi
-MetaWorld- claiming to be a web3/play-to-earn/crypto-game. It looked like something I can enjoy playing as it has 3D graphics. Vastly different from the other play-to-earn games I tried before. A lot of the other play-to-earn games were 2D and the earnings aren’t that substantial in terms of time and investment, aside from “Axie” which I started hearing about back in college and was skeptical off at the time. The YGG entity mentioned here in this document apparently started in that game as well. GensoKishi is a web3 port of a Japanese-exclusive MMORPG videogame called Elemental Knights Online. Web3 is a term used to describe videogames that incorporates cryptocurrencies. Some of the User Generated Contents from the web3 version gets put into the web2 version after winning contests. At first, I won 5$ from a raffle from them. It got me invested and when the game released, I played it and even made video contents about it from the perspective of a newbie in the web3 scene. Got recognition not just from the players/community but part of the moderation team of the game as well. My earnings from this game were about 10$/daily just by playing it alongside joining events and raffles about it. And even attended a in-real-life gathering hosted by them, got a USB Flash Drive and Power Bank with their logo as memorabilia.
References: youtu.be/watch?v=gRs_cEMXUBo&list=PLRcbi_hW-V3de6FgfVLGa3hotRPrVumWz&pp=sAgC

SEPT. 13, 2022 – MirkoTik Router Configuration
Set up my MikroTik hAP Lite to send an email notification to my email address upon anyone possibly trying to login to the WinBox which is the utility to configure the said router. My uncle who I lived with at this time used to be a professor of IT at a University so he has his own CCTV setup and so on using VCR etc.
Reference: facebook.com/share/v/1B4g8NCTWd/

after Jan. 16, 2022 – Grandparents’ Ancestral Home
This happened 2 years after my college graduation, after my first actual employment experience that culturally shocked me little a bit, which I guess was normal for that company of great significance. But also because of the COVID Pandemic causing me to stay at home beforehand as relatives advised and news of recruitments dropping because of people adjusting to the new normal of working from home. Reason for leaving was that I was really stressed from the aforementioned details and that there were now plenty of residents in the apartment’s complex and it was getting noisy. I was the first resident in that apartment complex, but probably second in reservation, witnessing the construction of the other parts of it. Couldn’t find any other nearby apartments to go to so opted to live with my uncle here in the ancestral home.

Jan. 16 2022 – Kara-O-Kruz, Published on Google Play
I did pay the developer account fee for this and later on, the app wasn’t really getting any traction so I just took it off until my developer account got suspended. No violations, mostly just due to in-activity. The app was priced at 1$ and wasn’t taking any data from users, merely a simulation of a that coin-toss game.
Reference: facebook.com/share/p/14b1ib4Ap6w/

May 22, 2022 – Getting into Pokemon TCG
Ever since I got back to my home country, wheneve I needed some cash I would sell some of my belongings. These goes as far back as the days of OLX.com or Sulit.ph or HanapUsapDeal websites. So I do this with items that I no longer need.
Reference: facebook.com/marketplace/profile/100055752107854/?product_id=5493322714025670

Dec. 7 2021 – Photo of My Employee ID
I resigned mainly because of the stress as mentioned above aside from having barely any experience with car’s ECUs. After leaving I asked if I would be able to come back if ever and my superior said that I may but only once. During the application process I took the time to read the contract and luckily, I was able to leave without having to pay them back for the training fees. This is where I learned about Training Bonds. You see, almost my entire young adult life since I was taught to read, write, even in cursive, and do math. I’ve been left alone mostly to study on my own… And I’m not really close to my father who would probably the one who would know these things better.
Reference: facebook.com/share/p/1Abakg1ua8/

Nov. 8, 2021 – Exam Results for DensoTen Employment
In the reference provided are my post about it and scores. The exam was done online, with strict rules to follow such as not alt-tabbing and keeping the operating system’s focus on the exam window. They wouldn’t want cheaters in this exam and I didn’t cheat. Not sure how complex their measures are for detecting cheating but this is a company mainly dealing with manufacturing Japanese Car Parts. And I wouldn’t want to find out what would happen if I cheated. I didn’t even know about the company before honestly. I just answered a Facebook Puzzle post and got messaged about it then went through the interviews and hiring process.
Reference: facebook.com/share/p/1DcDekvmNV/

May 15, 2021 – Addon for Elder Scrolls Online Videogame
Made and uploaded my very first add-on using APIs for Elder Scrolls Online. The addon is a simple text overlay depicting Experience Points gain and tracking with plenty of customization options. It is currently sitting at a total of 12,172 downloads with a monthly download rate of 61. I need to update this addon soon for the PlayStation Console Platform. Khayeel is a pen name I use for Programming Passion Projects. It is a lengthened and arabicized form of ‘KL’ which is ‘Kuya Lorman’ given by a high-school classmate.
Reference: esoui.com/downloads/info3072-XPTracker.html


Mar. 1, 2021 – Computer Books Collection Summary
I don’t’ really read much books anymore due to the internet. But back then, the kinds of books I would read are all about academics but I did start out with fairy tales too like “Turtle and the Hare”. When I got some allowance while studying in college, I would frequent the local second-hand bookstore for computer books. Just in case of an apocalyptic setting that we lose access to internet and some of our technologies today.
Reference: facebook.com/photo/?fbid=222921229576279

Dec. 27, 2020 – The Desktop PC I am Currently using
Right around the time of the COVID Pandemic, I decided that Laptop’s are just too flimsy for my use case and I had to get back on a Desktop PC. I started buying up parts second hand and brand new depending on my priorities. I didn’t cheap out on Power Supply, bought a second-hand GPU since I had experience with the buy-and-sell scene already. My first CPU + Ram Bundle was from my close high school friend who upgraded until I later on upgraded it as well. More about my other Desktop PC Builds further down these records.

May. 30, 2020 – Graduate from BSCS
Take note of how this is during the peak of the pandemic. Social gatherings are banned. My mother couldn’t come home from Saudi Arabia. Lost motivation to even attend the re-scheduled Graduation Ceremony. Went to the Registrar’s Office to claim my Diploma instead and surprisingly there was a medal in there which I tried to research on and only explanation I can find is that it is a St. Lorenzo Ruiz award but I am not sure.

Dec. 27 – May. 30, 2020 – College Organizations
Became an Auditor for SITES which is the Society of Information and Technology Engineering Students. Also became a staff of the College Student Council when my classmate won the election. On-The-Job Training at MISOUT. Leaving all other details that you can find on my LinkedIn profile. For the most part I was a sole developer in projects. The thesis we accomplished was my proposal. There were just 2 of us in our batch to graduate. That other student is a friend and I let him handle most of the documentation and writing while I do the theses project with a lot of help from him, but mostly the proposal was mine and when I did the proposal, I already had a plan of action as well, all that was left was to execute it. Website Development, availing of actual Web Hosting and buying Domain Names. Programming in SQL, connecting front-end to back-end and working on both. On our Mock-Theses project during 3rd year. I was the only proponent and what I did was a Point-of-Sale system as per the professor’s request of making them for different businesses. The Hardware Store POS task was given to me. Fortunately, my mom does have friends in this locality since it’s their hometown. That friend was my sister’s ‘Ninang’. I probably could have asked the professor as well if they know anyone, I can make a system for but I don’t remember. The system I presented came with a Barcode Scanner and a Thermal Receipt Printer. I even bought a Fingerprint Scanner and also planned to include a Cash Register and a Product Statistics View. But the only ones I got to work with the time I had was the Printer and the Barcode Scanner along with the basic functionalities of a POS and built-in event logging. This project is uploaded to my GitHub currently but outdated. The Mock-Theses went fine with Minor Revisions Advised such as not allowing direct editing into the product tables from the POS software. No second takes. For that project as well, we were able to meet up with the local supplier of POS to SM Taytay Hypermarket to help us get familiarized with the machine and software.

[CV additional details not yet in the old one or not yet organized]
Check date joined REImage Server and became an intern developer free of charge and was part of 1 pushed patch(task wass to change some item's max stack count and category).
Letterboxd(https://letterboxd.com/vsgamer57/films/)
Built a PC for Saus'/his younger brother somewhere during or before college?.
Had Astigmatism from liking wearing graded glasses of Classmates back in IPSA I guess -> Had Lasik Eye Surgery with my sister to have it fixed...
After-surgery my hand jerked almost involuntarily that it dislocated the \"flap\" so we had to call for emergency doctor from Shinagawa, even the doctor said that was very rare and not normal.
