MOVED RESIDENCE <- Had Lasik Eye Surgery & Learned a little basic Lock-picking, first time earning from crypto-currency through Electroneum
BEFORE DEC. 27, 2020 – BUKAL DOS, SMART CIR. EXT, TAYTAY
Lived here until Graduation from the course of Bachelor of Science in Computer Science majoring in programming/software development. Initially moved in here with my mom’s cousin’s family. Until about a year before my graduation which by then I was back to living by myself. Most memorable experiences are that I broke the metallic faucet by bumping into it with my knee and carrying the 1 Horse Power Air Conditioning Unit from the second floor down to the ground floor through a tight spiral staircase for cleaning then carrying it back up all by myself without any special tools. We moved here around my 3rd Year standing in my course. Around this time I went with colleagues in the Computer Engineering Dept. to be a 'mamamasa' during amba in taytay. Dual booted my laptop with ParrotOS.

MOVED RESIDENCE
ISAGANI STREET, TAYTAY, RIZAL - Started buying second hand computer books and collecting Pokémon Cards and Gundam Plastic Models
This is where I started living with my mom's cousin's family as guardians and when I started studying in Siena College of Taytay. During these time I got into Gundam Plastic Models and I would do that and make videos of it while going to college as my free time aside from the laptop. While studying, every feeling of winning in the classroom due to stuff like leaving laboratory first, I would go for Starbucks and just hang out while fiddling with my phone online, a little people=watching and good coffee. 2 Venti's of Caramel Macchiato with Breve Milk as suggested by the barista. I would sit there and smoke my cigs for like 5 hours or more even.

RESTART - This is actually where the Positive Directed Restart happened.
Finally got to talk to my mom again from Baguio and told her I would pursue my dream since childhood of becoming a programmer. That I needed her help and that I wouldn't fuck up again LMAO because of papi'LOVE'. Got her support, incredible right? Do I deserve this?

MOVED RESIDENCE
Baguio (Result of me giving up in life XD then decided might as well try to get the Diploma for the field I wanted.)
Moved into Baguio with aunt's family who had their clothing business there. Here I would for the first time experience a little selling of clothes despite swearing to myself that I abhor front-desk type of jobs as I don't think I am fluent enough to deal with certain types of people. Much prefer the company of a device + internet. During this time I was kind of already disassociated with my parents and family because I wasted the plane ticket that I was to board on during a female friend's debut birthday which I chose to attend instead... Got a scar on my right wrist for it because a ceramic plate was thrown at me that night I got home from the party.

MOVED RESIDENCE
20th Avenue, QC, Cubao - 1 STUDIO ROOM
Parents went for vacation in Philippines to see where I was staying and immediately decided to move me to a Studio Room nearby, closer to the college.
Got mind blown here when I tried to make a virtual clock as a project submission. LOL not knowing back then about what the CMOS battery was for exactly.

MOVED RESIDENCE
Cubao, Boarding House
Before the Academic Year started, went here with some friends to look for a place I can stay in while attending college/university and we found a boarding house. I lived here for a while, sharing bedroom with like 5+ industry workers mostly office jobs or Call Center Agents. Some of the students also opted to stay here. Made a close friend here.. Learned from them about the Sony Brand CellPhone Line and Custom Cellphone OSes or ROMS.

FRESHMAN SCHOLAR OF TIP CUBAO
My first choice of College or University was actually PUP or Polytechnical University of the Philippines but honestly I don't much about them, I was just going by what I could read about them. Went to Technological Institute of the Philippines, Cubao instead, since I learned that is where my Sienan high school friends were going. After the entrance examinations, I was qualified and availed of the scholarship. When asked what course I would take, I countered with a question asking what would be the hardest IT related course. So I took up, Electronics and Communications Engineering as my first course or ECE. The schedule was pretty rough as a block student with some going into like 7PM-8PM. By then I would even just sleep on my desk and the professor would allow picture taking or joke about it I guess. Didn't help that our little friend group loves cutting classes to the computer shop...

MOVED RESIDENCE - Beverly Hills, Antipolo
From living by myself in the latter stages of living in Little Baguio, Taytay, Rizal to moving into my Aunt's Mansion @ Beverly Hills, Antipolo.
4th Year Homeschooling in which took me 2 years to eventually want to even try college.

SIENA COLLEGE OF TAYTAY AS A HIGHSCHOOLER 2009
Was part of the dance troupe during the Sportsfest. Only stayed here for 1 year.
Reference: youtube.com/watch?v=6TreBLUQ_FM, I was the one who jumped at the back near the end..
Some classmates would wonder I guess how am I passing subject when I mostly just sleep in class because I am always up at the apartment on my computer. Lost all motivation in society at this point. Wondering whether if I actually made friends at all or not in the past. Maybe I just didn't know the social landscape that well as an innocent kind hearted friendly almost ma-epal na kid in my previous schools, that all changed here. I started keeping to myself as much as possible and my friends from here now are actually the ones who came up to me to get to know me... My headspace that time was just, I'mma try all these things they don't want us to try just to see why do people do these things. I already started smoking anyway. So alcohol, women and maybe even a little drugs. Thankfully though, I never got into rocks. LOL. But despite these I would confront my friends from here as a pretentious cool guy, I was more like just a financer to the drinking sessions and we would talk about stuff and I would always remind them to be skeptic about why things are the way they are.. We were all young but I was like the eldest so I felt a little bit of responsibility too... It is a treasure all the stuff we came up with in our talks and bonding... FOSFOS - Friends Of Saus

MOVED RESIDENCE - R. Valle, Little Baguio, Taytay, Rizal
After exiting Saudi Arabia as a 3rd Year High School Drop Out, starting living here with my younger sister, some uncles and a maid. Continued High Schooling in Siena College of Taytay where I met my most recent closest friends eva~!
Because we would drink alcohol almost after every after school. Even got blacklisted out of 4th Year HS for this... So did homeschooling at Victory Elijah Schooling Systems instead at Mambugan, Antipolo?, Rizal. Around this time was when I was also assisting mom in the papers for the properties she wanted. It was always her dream to have her own House & Lot and she got it by her own efforts and some help from the facilitators/processors of course as part of process. All that's left is for us to actually live together in it... This is also around the time Facebook become more popular so I made my first account here which later got banned for Copyright Issue of Streaming Anime. Currently on my second Facebook Account. Making accounts back then wasn't that 'secure' was even aware of quick email account makers back then through a website called DarkYahoo.Net(first learned about it from high school students in IPSA). The first personal PC Desktop I built for myself as a gift from my mom and dad was with me here, brought from Saudi Arabia where we bought and built it. After getting blacklisted from 4th Year of HighSchool at Siena I started playing this video game Shin Megami Tensei: Imagine Online and this is where I met a Japanese IT Guy, Aki Asai. Until now we are still in connection but barely talk to each other, most recent was like a few days ago. He inspired me to do better when I told him I wanted to be in his shoes. \"I want you to be better than me.\" Something like that. Ain't that the best advice you can respond with right? Poor fella's still not settling down until now damn it LMAO... Just grateful he's still there.

IPSA, Alkhobar - Sections; Noble then requested to transfer to Humility because GF was there.
 Studied 1st Year High School until I dropped out on the middle of 3rd Year due to papi loves LOL
No issue whatsoever as far as I know in terms of academics. Maybe some professors or school staff would have something to say, Got called in to Guidance Counseling for not greeting the Councillor around the same time I guess that I had a girlfriend here. First time reaction upon moving to this school was like \"Why are the girls screaming upon seeing me?\" I was slender and features like collarbone and jawline.. already started growing some mustache here I think. Choreographed some dances here as well but cannot really remember being part of the Dance Troupe, I did audition for it IIRC. This is also where I learned to play some Guitar and Read Tabs/Chords off of UltimateGuitar.com . Battle of the Bands here are fun. A lot of the students here are into Punk Rock and it's variants. Afte dropping out of highschool here. I would sneak out at night to go to the nearby computer shop and one night I happen to pick up a sealed Davidoff Cigarette Pack and just started smoketh'! Been addicted to it since and even tried vaping now but nope, I am currently looking into natural tobacco tough. Was tasked to translate and write a script from Tagalog to Baybayin for the Filipino Month Decorations.

MOVED RESIDENCES
Alkhobar, SAUDI ARABIA from Jeddah due to dad's work starting at SECUTRONIC.
For the first academic year moving here, I was late for enrollment so I didn't go to school yet and was held back by a year. Somehow that also attributed to my diagnosis of Extreme Depression around this time as all I can think about was the girlfriend I left behind in Jeddah... I could have died here if the wind blew me off the edge of the rooftop of that 8 story apartment flats... Had a little booklet about KungFu and I would try to read and practice it in my free time. The trigger for the mental illness was that one night. I heard rushing footsteps around our rooftop flat. But when I chased to see where I couldn't see them. I was worried somehow that there were people peeping on us and such so I told my parents and I was like hyperventilating that time and eventually thought they wouldn't believe me so I rushed out into the streets trying to chase the voices I was hearing until they took me by car and brought me to the hospital where I was confied while being diagnosed. Tried to punch a male nurse here in the process... While confined I was having delusions/visions of my sister in danger. Not knowing what's real or not, I would rather do all I can in my power to ensure that everything is okay so I would scream at the top of my lungs and bang on everything everytime I am awake so they had to sedate me to sleep. The diagnosis then was Extreme Depression and while under the influence of the medicines, I would see people's aura's/colors and even felt like I could understand their languages. Weird. We got into a church community here and I also started attending Legion of Mary here with the other Philippine School Students. Plenty of Chruch Activities, weekly and yearly. Even got to dance like in a ballroom with the girlfriend I had here but as a chruch performance... One Way Jesus!~ Found out about DTXMania, the Drum Simulation Arcade Game here as a Computer Software. And that the highschool batch I was originally supposed to be in as tech-savvy as well, even more so as they were the ones to show me stuff like, Operating Systems on an External Harddrive. The website DarkYahoo.Net and Custom Windows/OS Boot Logos. Si kuya Yuri... This is also where I was cicrcumcised in a hospital under anaesthesia with lasers- yeah it's a different method there- as I requested because I was teased by a gurl at the previous location for being un-so. LOL. Knot-tying Champion. Itachi cosplayer as campaign manager for my girlfriend at the time who was running for PRO. Dad taught us how to fish without Rod, shore spear-crabbing, and some basic electronics and components concepts like AC and DC. Some I already know since he did have me as ajunior tainee at the previous company. Got to ride on a big ATV at the Desert.

IPSJ, Jeddah
Grade 5 - Grade 6 - Sections; Del Pilar
The music culture here is more R&B, HipHop and Rap. The first time ever I felt something weird that I believed was love. Her name flashed before my eyes while we were walking in the streets near the school and all of a sudden my heart started beating 'loudly'. Couldn't explain it but the next time I saw her I was like 'smiling'? At first she kinda shooed me off but eventually, I knocked on their class' door during a lecture and sent a love letter then that's it.
Still don't know much about this whole gf/bf thing honestly. Other pairs were already kissing in front of us LMAO. Math competition contestant. 3rd Placer English Declamation.

Jeddah Reef Int'l School
Grade 3 and Grade 4
Pakistani friend who showed me how passwords should be- with symbols and even incomprehensible. First time seeing Sandstorm. Mom was a computer/english teacher here while I was a student. Got jealous of a guy's hair being so straight and just like how Trunks has his hair. All of a sudden hair is a big deal because there's this one guy who loves making this gesture of swiping his hands across his forehead to his hair. So I started using Hairstyling gel a lot more too. LOL. Top2

MOVED RESIDENCES
JEDDAH, SAUDI ARABIA
Finally my Dad brought us with him to abroad, me, my mom and my sister. Apparently my dad was doing a side-business here as Media Discs Private Peddler. CDs Burning/Copying of Movies, Audio Discs, Concerts, etc.. We had a 3 storey cabinet filled to the brim with these. And I would watch whatever I felt like watching from these. Guess he downloaded these stuff from his showroom at Alesayi&AlsawadiGroup where he worked as a Board Level Electrionics Technician. Due to the difference in Academic Timelines int he Philippines and Saudi Arabia, I was also held back a year in here upon moving. So I would help mom deliver food as catering service to my dad's coworkers as dad's work was at a mall just accross the road from our residence. Then eventually dad would let me train as a junior in that company, fixing computer power supplies and assembling desktop PCs, guided by dad's indian and bangladesh coworker, Shakeed and I forgot the other guy's name, that guy is more disciplined while Shakeeb is a wild Degenerate but funny LMFAO, Shakeeb is fine, just makulit paminsan hahaha nothing bad actually happened LOL. Got addicted to Albaik broasted chicken, it was jsut behind our residence. Loved the nuggets and fries. Mom found a CD that contains flirtatious remarks to a woman supposedly in London supposedly by Dad. Mom got furious because dad was her first ever at all. He almost stabbed him so I hid all the sharp objects at the kitchen and talked to mom about it... She also threw/thrashed the CD Collections at him. Also the first time I encountered porn both from home and school, yeah, found my dad's stash LOL. Internet connection during this time was still throgh the telephone and Cards you had to redeem. Dad taught me about Google Searching around this time. Dad taught us a little self-defense such as katas and forms. He filled a soccerball with sand and hung it for us to hit.

